WO-10: C2 replay/inject verification -- does inject_forged_rc_override move
the vessel's TRUE Gazebo position, not just what MAVLink reports?

Boot method (full stack, native Gazebo/VRX, no docker):
  1. sim_config/start_vrx.sh (headless VRX/Gazebo, sydney_regatta world,
     wamv_ardupilot.sdf) -- confirmed up via "Publishing dynamic pose
     messages on [/world/sydney_regatta/dynamic_pose/info]".
  2. attacks/gps_spoof.py run with spoofing left OFF (pure passthrough
     relay, 9002 <-> 9100) -- confirmed bound: "GPS spoof relay: bound
     ('127.0.0.1', 9002), Gazebo at ('127.0.0.1', 9100)". Run with stdin
     wired to a FIFO held open by a keepalive writer, so control_cli's
     input() blocks quietly instead of spinning or hitting EOF.
  3. ArduPilot SITL invoked directly (build/sitl/bin/ardurover --model
     JSON --speedup 1 --slave 0 --sim-address=127.0.0.1 -I0 --home
     -33.724223,150.679736,0.0,0.0), bypassing sim_vehicle.py/MAVProxy,
     which needs a real tty and exits immediately without one (confirmed:
     MAVProxy connected, printed "MAV>", unloaded all modules, exited).
     SITL bound SERIAL0 on tcp:5760.
  4. A standalone MAVLink fan-out bridge (this session's scratch script,
     not yet committed -- this is exactly what WO-14's run_sim.sh should
     formalize) connects to tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 as the sole GCS, requests
     MAV_DATA_STREAM_ALL, and mirrors traffic bidirectionally to the
     three UDP endpoints this project's scripts already expect: 14551
     (dashboard), 14552 (auto_mission), 14553 (c2_replay). Verified: a
     client on udpin:127.0.0.1:14551 received HEARTBEAT and
     GLOBAL_POSITION_INT immediately.

Test method:
  Connected on 14553 (attacks/c2_replay.py's own connect()), set MANUAL
  mode and armed (ARMED STATE: True). Captured the vessel's TRUE Gazebo
  position independently of MAVLink, using the same gz-topic technique
  nodes/ais_emulator/ais_emulator.py uses (subscribe to
  /world/sydney_regatta/dynamic_pose/info, parse the wamv block), both
  before and after calling attacks/c2_replay.py's real
  inject_forged_rc_override(conn, throttle_pwm=1800, steering_pwm=1500,
  duration_s=10.0) unmodified.

Methodology pitfall found and fixed: a first pass read GLOBAL_POSITION_INT
via a single recv_match() call immediately after the override loop. Result
was byte-identical lat/lon before and after (dlat=dlon=0.0000000) --
inject_forged_rc_override's 10s loop only sends RC_CHANNELS_OVERRIDE and
never drains incoming telemetry, so ~10s of GLOBAL_POSITION_INT messages
piled up in the UDP socket buffer; a single recv_match() pops the OLDEST
queued message, not the latest, making it look like nothing moved. Fixed
by draining the buffer for 1.5s and keeping the last message seen
(latest_global_position() helper) before trusting the reading. This was a
test-script artifact, not a product bug -- noting it here since it would
silently produce a false negative if repeated at Checkpoint 1.

Result (corrected run):
  TRUE Gazebo position before:  (-533.180, 161.394, -0.031)
  TRUE Gazebo position after:   (-534.797, 161.586, -0.158)
  TRUE Gazebo displacement:     dx=-1.617m, dy=0.191m, dist=1.628m

  MAVLink GLOBAL_POSITION_INT before: lat=-33.7227731, lon=150.6739773
  MAVLink GLOBAL_POSITION_INT after:  lat=-33.7227739, lon=150.6739651
  MAVLink-reported displacement: dlat=-0.0000008 deg (~0.09m),
                                  dlon=-0.0000122 deg (~1.13m at this
                                  latitude)

  Both readings agree in sign and rough magnitude on the dominant
  east-west component (TRUE dx=-1.617m west; MAVLink dlon corresponds to
  ~1.13m west) -- independently confirming the vessel's TRUE Gazebo
  position moved as a direct result of inject_forged_rc_override, matching
  the docstring's claim ("should move the vessel's TRUE Gazebo position,
  not just its believed one"). CONFIRMED.

Ground truth log: attack_logs/c2_replay_ground_truth.csv gained the
matching row:
  inject_rc_override,"throttle=1800, steering=1500, 10.0s"

GPS/AIS/C2 not re-checked together in this pass (that's Checkpoint 1,
which still waits on WO-11 through WO-13). This closes out the one
specific gap WO-10 targeted.
